--decomposition-review \\\"$D\\\" completed\\n# goal 1\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html current-state -p 2.1: \\\"No button-chain.html exists in this proof. Goal 01 owns only planned future targets W01-W04 and does not create files during this benchmark run.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html why -p 4.1: \\\"The future page behavior depends on a precise load state, visual stacking, append rule, and completion rule. Keeping these as separate work units prevents the off-by-one completion behavior from being hidden inside broad implementation wording.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html scope -p 5.1: \\\"In scope for future execution: one HTML document body subtree, one button style selector, appendNextButton(), and finishDocument(). Out of scope: tests, browser execution, extra controls, persistence, counters displayed to the user, or alternative completion text.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html affected -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected file is button-chain.html. The markup, style, append function, and finish function are independently reviewable targets in that single file.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html dependencies -p 7.1: \\\"W01 has no dependency. W02 depends on W01. W03 depends on W01 and W02. W04 depends on W03. Goal 02 can rely on these contracts for proof planning.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html approach-risks -p 8.1: \\\"Use a generated count that distinguishes generated buttons from the initial button. Only the last button receives active append behavior; older buttons must be inert for appending. The fourth generated button must be identifiable and must call finishDocument() when pressed.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \\\"Not applicable; this goal owns four work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\\\"\\n# goal 2\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff current-state -p 2.1: \\\"No tests or browser runs are executed during this planning-only proof. Goal 02 records the future proof targets that an executor must run after creating button-chain.html.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff why -p 4.1: \\\"The task is interactive and easy to satisfy incorrectly through an off-by-one chain, missing border, or non-last-button append behavior. Separate DOM and browser proof work units make these failures observable.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff scope -p 5.1: \\\"In scope for future execution: one DOM interaction test target and one real browser story run. Out of scope for this proof: running those commands, opening HTML, or marking the UI story passed.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff affected -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected proof file is button-chain.test.js. Browser story evidence belongs in ui-story-runs/US-01.md after implementation, not during this proof.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff dependencies -p 7.1: \\\"W05 depends on W01-W04. W06 depends on W01-W05 so the browser story runs after automated assertions exist. Completion handoff is the DOM test result plus US-01 browser evidence.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff approach-risks -p 8.1: \\\"The DOM test must assert exact counts after each click and final computed/visible border evidence. The browser story must use real clicks only and must not use console evaluation, storage mutation, or injected events.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --goal-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff goal-size-exception -p 11.1: \\\"Not applicable; this goal owns two work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\\\"\\n# step sections\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/01-step-initial-markup instructions -p 5.1: \\\"Future executor creates button-chain.html with a minimal valid HTML document and a body subtree containing exactly one button element at load. The button should be identifiable as the initial/current last button and should not be accompanied by finished text or generated-button placeholders.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/01-step-initial-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\"Loading the future file before interaction exposes exactly one visible button and zero elements or text nodes whose rendered content equals finished.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/01-step-initial-markup handoff -p 7.1: \\\"W02 and W03 can rely on a single initial button existing as the only chain control at load.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/02-step-button-layout-style instructions -p 5.1: \\\"Future executor styles .chain-button so each generated button is displayed as its own visible row below the previous button, with enough spacing for a user to identify and click the current last button.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/02-step-button-layout-style acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\"After generated buttons are appended, their visual order matches DOM order and no style causes overlap, hidden buttons, or ambiguous last-button targeting.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/02-step-button-layout-style handoff -p 7.1: \\\"W03 can rely on visible stacked buttons for last-button interaction, and W06 can use bottom-most visible button targeting.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/03-step-append-handler instructions -p 5.1: \\\"Future executor implements appendNextButton() so a click on the current last button appends exactly one new button after it, updates current-last ownership to the new button, and prevents earlier buttons from appending additional buttons. Generated-button numbering must count generated buttons only.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/03-step-append-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\"From load, click 1 on the initial button creates generated button 1; click 2 on generated 1 creates generated 2; click 3 on generated 2 creates generated 3; click 4 on generated 3 creates generated 4. Each click increases the button count by exactly one and older non-last buttons do not append.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/03-step-append-handler handoff -p 7.1: \\\"W04 can rely on generated button 4 existing only after the fourth append-producing click and being the current last button.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/04-step-finish-handler instructions -p 5.1: \\\"Future executor implements finishDocument() so pressing generated button 4 clears all prior document body content and renders one completion element containing exactly finished in lowercase with a visible white border.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/04-step-finish-handler acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\"Click 5 from the initial state, performed on generated button 4, leaves no buttons in the document and renders exact visible text finished with a nonzero visible white border. No other casing, extra text, or remaining chain content is accepted.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 01-button-chain-html/04-step-finish-handler handoff -p 7.1: \\\"W05 and W06 can assert the five-click sequence and final completion state.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff/01-step-dom-test instructions -p 5.1: \\\"Future executor adds button-chain.test.js using the repository-appropriate DOM testing harness. The test loads button-chain.html, performs real DOM click dispatches against the current last button, checks counts after each append, verifies prior buttons do not append, then clicks generated button 4 and checks the final body content and border style.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff/01-step-dom-test acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\"The test fails unless the initial button count is one, clicks 1-4 append exactly one button each, click 5 on generated button 4 removes all buttons, body text is exactly finished, and the completion element has a visible white border.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff/01-step-dom-test handoff -p 7.1: \\\"W06 can rely on the DOM test command and results as pre-browser evidence, but still must run the real browser story separately.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff/02-step-browser-story instructions -p 5.1: \\\"Future executor runs US-01 with normal browser input only. Load the local file, click the bottom-most visible button five times from the initial state, and record the URL/file path, visible button count progression, final screenshot or observation, exact text, and visible white border evidence.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff/02-step-browser-story acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \\\"US-01 passes only when the browser evidence shows one initial button, exactly one appended button after each of the first four clicks, and after the fifth click only finished remains with a visible white border. It remains untested during this planning-only proof.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --step-section \\\"$D\\\" 02-proof-and-handoff/02-step-browser-story handoff -p 7.1: \\\"Completion handoff is the updated ui-story-runs/US-01.md evidence and no open bugs in bugs.md.\\\"\\n'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\n{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_37\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/bash -lc 'set -e\\nP=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T205844Z-clean-current-seeded-fresh/current/worker/planning\\nD=basic-test-proof-current-20260811t205844z-clean-current-seeded-fresh-isolated-plan\\nexport PLANS_ROOT=$PWD\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --description-section \\\"$D\\\" current-state -p 2.1: \\\"The isolated benchmark workspace contains only the benchmark prompt inputs and generated plan artifacts. No implementation files exist for the future task, and this proof must not create or inspect HTML, start a browser, serve files, or execute UI tooling. The tagged planning skill source is $P/SKILL.md with repository-local UI reference references/ui-user-story-validation.md.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --description-section \\\"$D\\\" desired-outcome -p 3.1: \\\"Produce a durable implementation plan for a future button-chain.html task. The future deliverable loads with exactly one initial button; clicking only the current last button appends exactly one new button below it; after the fourth generated button exists, pressing that fourth generated button clears the document and renders exact lowercase text finished with a visible white border.\\\"\\n\\\"$P/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\\\" --description-section \\\"$D\\\" approach -p 4.1: \\\"Plan fro